{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":264070,"duration_api_ms":263998,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development. It derives formal specs from C source code of GNU utilities, generates Go implementations from those specs, and verifies parity against reference binaries through differential testing. The goal is to characterize where the AI code generation methodology holds and where it breaks.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility implementations, `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform-divergent syscalls, `pkg/format/` handles output formatting. Build via Mage targets; verification via `go test` comparing Go binaries against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Current Implementation**: Source code exists for `pkg/testutils` (difftest.go, normalize.go), `cmd/ts` (main.go, ts_test.go), `cmd/cat` (main.go, cat_test.go), `cmd/wc` (main.go, wc_test.go), and `cmd/sponge` (main.go only — **sponge_test.go is missing**). `pkg/sys/` and `pkg/format/` have PRDs but no implementation code yet.\n\n**Current Release**: rel01.0 (in_progress) has all code artifacts present (ts implementation + tests + testutils). The next clear gap is in rel01.1: `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` does not exist, while all other rel01.1 utilities (wc, cat) already have their differential test files.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nrel01.0 has all code artifacts in place. The earliest actionable code gap is `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` in rel01.1. This is the single missing test file across all four rel01.x utilities. It depends on `pkg/testutils` (already implemented) and `cmd/sponge/main.go` (already implemented). No other code must be built first.\n\nSponge tests are uniquely challenging because sponge's primary output is a file, not stdout. The standard `RunDiffTests` harness runs both binaries in the same working directory, which means the reference binary would overwrite the Go binary's output file. File-output test cases need a custom helper that runs each binary in its own isolated directory.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/sponge differential tests -- prd007-sponge R6, prd001-testutils R5\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd007-sponge.yaml (R6 differential testing requirements)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (R1-R3 harness API, R5 file-state comparison)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.1.yaml (sponge test case definitions -- 8 cases)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc003-sponge.yaml (use case flow and success criteria)\n      - cmd/sponge/main.go (implementation under test)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (harness: DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, FileExpectation, executeBinary)\n      - pkg/testutils/normalize.go (NormalizeFunc, ComposeNormalizers)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (pattern reference for TestMain, fixture setup, and RunDiffTests usage)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (pattern reference for file-based test fixtures with WorkDir)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Differential tests for cmd/sponge exercising all 8 sponge test cases from test-rel01.1.yaml\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement TestMain following the pattern in cmd/cat/cat_test.go: build the Go sponge\n          binary into a temp directory via \"go build -o <path> .\", locate the Homebrew reference\n          binary \"sponge\" (brew install moreutils) via exec.LookPath(\"sponge\"), and set\n          package-level goBinary and refBinary variables. Clean up the temp directory after\n          m.Run(). Per prd007-sponge R6 and sources.yaml (moreutils utilities are not g-prefixed).\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement a runFileDiffTest helper function for file-output test cases. The standard\n          RunDiffTests harness runs both binaries in the same working directory, so the reference\n          binary would overwrite the Go binary's output file. The helper must: (a) create two\n          isolated temp directories with identical fixture files via a setupFixture callback,\n          (b) run the Go binary in directory 1 with the given stdin, args, and env using\n          exec.CommandContext with a 10-second timeout, (c) run the reference binary in directory\n          2 with identical inputs, (d) compare stdout and stderr from both binaries byte-for-byte,\n          (e) compare exit codes, (f) read the output file from both directories and compare their\n          content byte-for-byte, (g) on divergence report: args, stdin (truncated to 256 bytes),\n          both file contents, both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes. Per prd007-sponge\n          R6.1 and prd001-testutils R5.1-R5.2.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement three basic file-output test cases using runFileDiffTest:\n          (a) sponge_small_stdin_to_file -- generate 100 lines (\"1\\n\" through \"100\\n\") as stdin,\n          args [\"outfile.txt\"], no fixture setup needed. Traces prd007-sponge R1.1, R1.2, R2.1.\n          (b) sponge_soak_before_write -- create fixture data.txt containing \"line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n\"\n          in both directories, stdin is the same content, args [\"data.txt\"]. Output file must not\n          be empty or truncated. Traces prd007-sponge R1.1, R2.5.\n          (c) sponge_empty_stdin -- empty stdin ([]byte{}), args [\"empty_out.txt\"], no fixture.\n          Output file should be zero bytes. Traces prd007-sponge R1.1, R2.1.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement sponge_passthrough_stdout test case using RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils\n          (standard stdout comparison). Stdin is []byte(\"hello world\\n\"), args is nil (no output\n          filename). Both binaries should write stdin content to stdout. Per test-rel01.1.yaml\n          sponge_passthrough_stdout, tracing prd007-sponge R4.1, R4.3.\n      - id: R5\n        text: |\n          Implement two append-mode test cases using runFileDiffTest:\n          (a) sponge_append_mode -- create fixture existing.txt containing \"original line\\n\" in\n          both directories. Stdin \"appended line\\n\", args [\"-a\", \"existing.txt\"]. Output files\n          should contain \"original line\\nappended line\\n\". Traces prd007-sponge R3.1, R3.3.\n          (b) sponge_append_mode_no_existing_file -- no fixture, stdin \"new content\\n\", args\n          [\"-a\", \"newfile.txt\"]. Output files should contain \"new content\\n\". Traces\n          prd007-sponge R3.2.\n      - id: R6\n        text: |\n          Implement sponge_large_stdin test case using runFileDiffTest: generate a payload of\n          1,048,576+ bytes using bytes.Repeat of a known pattern as stdin, args [\"large_out.txt\"],\n          no fixture. Compare output file content from both directories. This exercises the\n          temp-file spill path. Per test-rel01.1.yaml sponge_large_stdin, tracing prd007-sponge\n          R1.3, R1.4.\n      - id: R7\n        text: |\n          Implement sponge_output_file_exists_mode test case using runFileDiffTest: create fixture\n          protected.txt with os.WriteFile using mode 0640 and content \"old content\\n\" in both\n          directories. Stdin \"new content\\n\", args [\"protected.txt\"]. Compare output file content\n          from both directories AND verify the file mode is 0640 in both directories using\n          os.Stat. Per test-rel01.1.yaml sponge_output_file_exists_mode, tracing prd007-sponge\n          R2.3.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Per prd007-sponge R6.1: \"Differential tests must compare the content of the output file\n          (not stdout) after both the Go binary and the reference binary have exited.\" The standard\n          RunDiffTests harness runs both binaries sequentially in the same working directory, which\n          means the reference binary would overwrite the Go binary's output file. File-output test\n          cases use a custom runFileDiffTest helper that creates two isolated temp directories --\n          one per binary -- with identical fixtures, runs each binary in its own directory, and\n          compares the output files from both directories.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Per test-rel01.1.yaml preconditions: \"each test creates an isolated temp directory\" and\n          \"Comparison is on output file content (prd001-testutils R5) for tests with an output\n          filename. Passthrough mode tests compare stdout byte-for-byte.\" Use RunDiffTests from\n          pkg/testutils for the passthrough test only; use runFileDiffTest for all seven\n          file-output tests.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Per sources.yaml moreutils section: \"Installs without g-prefix (ts, sponge, pee, vidir,\n          chronic) because these utilities do not conflict with any macOS built-ins.\" The reference\n          binary is located via exec.LookPath(\"sponge\"), not \"gsponge\".\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Follow the TestMain pattern from cmd/cat/cat_test.go: build Go binary into os.MkdirTemp,\n          locate reference binary via exec.LookPath, run m.Run(), clean up with os.RemoveAll. Tests\n          skip gracefully with t.Skip when either binary is unavailable.\n      - id: D5\n        text: |\n          Per test-rel01.1.yaml preconditions: \"All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent\n          divergence.\" Set baseEnv to []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"} and pass it to all test cases.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: |\n          All 8 sponge test cases from test-rel01.1.yaml are implemented: sponge_small_stdin_to_file,\n          sponge_soak_before_write, sponge_passthrough_stdout, sponge_append_mode,\n          sponge_append_mode_no_existing_file, sponge_large_stdin, sponge_output_file_exists_mode,\n          sponge_empty_stdin.\n      - id: AC2\n        text: |\n          File-output test cases run each binary in an isolated temp directory and compare the\n          output file content from both directories byte-for-byte.\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          The passthrough test (sponge_passthrough_stdout) uses RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils\n          with standard stdout comparison.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          The permission preservation test (sponge_output_file_exists_mode) verifies that the\n          output file mode is 0640 after both binaries execute.\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\n      - id: AC6\n        text: |\n          Tests skip gracefully with t.Skip when the Go binary cannot be built or the reference\n          sponge binary is not found on PATH.\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"29641d3f-feeb-4aee-b1a5-c0cd56516b10","total_cost_usd":1.1081737500000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":113245,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"output_tokens":15644,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":113245,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15644,"cacheReadInputTokens":18565,"cacheCreationInputTokens":113245,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1081737500000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"65f4926e-9072-4a39-b2ae-5b2c00028fb4"}
